0. DEFINITIONS
   A "Development Installation" is an installation that is not
   publicly accessible: your own computer, or a staging server that
   only a restricted circle can reach (for example password
   protected). A "Public Site" is any installation that is not a
   Development Installation.

1. GRANT
   The licensor grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable right to
   use Jaco CMS free of charge on Development Installations and on
   Public Sites, including the operation of commercial websites you
   build with it, on your own servers or servers rented by you. Jaco
   contains no licence validation and phones home never.

2. FUTURE VERSIONS AND PAID LICENCES
   Development Installations stay free. For Public Sites, future
   versions may require a paid licence; any such version states its
   own update window (the period during which it includes new
   releases). Nothing in this licence promises that future versions
   will be free of charge.

